<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lambaréné</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lambaréné is a town in west-central Gabon on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ogooue">Ogooué River</a>, capital of Moyen-Ogooué province. In 1913 the Alsatian doctor and theologian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-schweitzer">Albert Schweitzer</a> founded a hospital at the Protestant mission there, which he ran for most of the rest of his life and for which he became widely known, receiving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> for 1952. The Albert Schweitzer Hospital still operates.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lambarene.jpg" alt="Lambaréné" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oshilumbu5 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lambarene1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
